  "tagline": "Event-sourced local-first data layer: reactive SQLite on the client, rebuilt from a synced event log.",
  "description": "LiveStore is a TypeScript state-management and sync framework that keeps app state in a reactive SQLite database on the client (WASM in browsers, native in React Native and Expo) and derives it from an append-only log of events. Events sync through pluggable backends such as Cloudflare Durable Objects, ElectricSQL or S2, and every client replays them through materializers to rebuild its SQLite tables, so conflicts are resolved by rebasing events rather than merging rows. It suits apps that want instant local queries, offline support and an audit-friendly event history. It is pre-1.0 and its APIs still change between releases.",
